

  JuyiHall collaboration flow contract
    √ starts OAuth before any protected hall load or background activity
    √ uses the stage header as the primary action surface without the duplicate dock
    √ distributes discussion entry points across courtyard bounty board and task cards
    √ uses in-scene objects as click targets without visible labels or highlight overlays
    √ keeps bounty panel opening isolated from map drag and enter flicker
    √ assigns a bounty to an explicit agent instead of hidden selectedAgent only
    √ keeps funded-bounty preview wiring capability-gated without changing map and roster boundaries
    √ keeps persistent command templates out of chat
    √ keeps both agent and task context in outgoing chat metadata
    √ sends hall messages with durable public bounty and private conversation scopes
    √ loads hall messages by conversation scope instead of the latest juyiting conversation only
    √ keeps bounty discussion scoped to assignees and private task chat separate
    √ opens the courtyard discussion entrance as a fresh public discussion by default
    √ uses separate discussion panels instead of one cross-scope chat interface
    √ limits hall chat mention choices to owned roster agents
    √ supports task management actions from the bounty board
    √ keeps low-value SongJiang and coordination panels out of the primary hall surface
    √ keeps low-value SongJiang and coordination actions out of chat panel
    √ shows an overflow hint when more than twelve agents are available
    √ keeps the portrait home as a shared-state presentation shell with separate map and roster flows
    √ keeps roster status filtering independent from map agents
    √ splits hall stage, data, and conversation responsibilities into dedicated units

  Juyi Hall conversation material references
    √ shows task-scoped fixed versions from the real task directory without turning them into chat text
    √ keeps legacy execution support but limits the embedded entrance to file browsing

  1.13.2 Babao-box workspace entry
    √ renders only canonical private output references and never promotes them to formal acceptance
    √ accepts only a published task artifact with an authoritative formal state and preserves no secrets
    √ uses the server taskId without a selected task and refuses a conflicting or missing published taskId (47ms)
    √ shows TASK publication lag as syncing rather than a pseudo-delivery
    √ drops malformed or secret-bearing conversation items and clears a stale request after a conversation switch
    √ offers version-pinned workspace references inline while retaining the Babao entry

